{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 1782 patchset-3 LLM review disposition and patchset-4 remediation:\n\nThe sole new advisory was valid: classify_paths has a fail-closed duplicate-path branch that parse_paths malformed-byte tests cannot reach. Added a direct duplicate of a valid documentation path to the full-route parametrization. No inline comments were unresolved. Earlier advisories remain dispositioned as recorded: classifier CLI and real composite-action selector tests were added; classification remains ahead of full jobs to avoid consuming the full runner graph for docs-only changes; classifier failure still blocks Verified while triggering full fallback to preserve fail-closed integrity.\n\nThree-stage review: spec compliance PASS (all documented fail-closed categories map to implementation/tests; architecture constraints preserved); code quality PASS (direct behavioral regression, no production expansion); domain integrity PASS/N/A (workflow route strings are boundary outputs, no new domain state or primitive-identity leak).\n\nPatchset 4: d3c0e6f257. Post-rebase validation: 213 focused classifier/workflow tests passed; make lint and actionlint passed; commit hooks including full mypy passed; GITHUB_REPOSITORY=navapbc/rebar complexity lock passed. Pushed immediately to Gerrit for renewed LLM-Review and Verified."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786731206423714001,"uuid":"8f5b9934-a8e1-4415-af1d-2b72d9a38b22"}